La Preneuse is a small public beach on the coast at Black River. It is named after the French frigate *Preneuse* which sailed from the island in the 18th century. It faces west across the open sea which makes it a quiet local place to watch the sunset.

On the beach stands the Martello tower a round stone fort built by the British in 1832 and 1833 and now a museum.

## Good to know

- The beach is smaller and calmer than Flic en Flac. Come for the evening light rather than a long day on the sand.
